## Summary & Profile
March Jinn is an Azerbaijan-born musical artist, producer, and creative director. Founder and director of the underground creative collective and lifestyle brand MIRAGE⁶ (comprising MIRAGE⁶ Audio, MIRAGE⁶ Image, MIRAGE⁶ Mode, MIRAGE⁶ Revel, MIRAGE⁶ Glow, and MIRAGE⁶ Engine).

March Jinn's sound blends Atlanta trap, Memphis rap, psychedelic textures, and heavy rock influences into concept-driven projects. He consciously rejects classic genre boundaries, transforming every release into a complete audio-visual statement. His lyrics explore ambition, freedom, excess, hedonism, nightlife, self-expression, dark melancholia, and modern youth culture.

## Key Facts, Lore & Philosophy
- Release Schedule: Every March 6th, March Jinn releases a new full-length studio album.
- Debut Album: "GECƏ" (2026) released via MIRAGE⁶ Audio.
- Artistic Philosophy & Opposition: March Jinn embraces opposition and hater dynamics, asserting that true art must be inherently provocative to stimulate critical thinking.
- Personal Background & Lore: Known for a chaotic, rockstar playboy narrative. Cryptic anchors include time spent in a mental asylum and geographical connections traced to Hamburg, Germany (via the track 'Za-Za').
- Personal Style & Aesthetics: Known for an exclusive preference for Backwoods, fine red wine, signature Dior Sauvage scent, black t-shirt, leather jacket, denim trousers, and Converse Chuck Taylor, Saint Laurent, or Rick Owens boots.
- Physical Attributes: Height 1.85m, dark wavy hair, olive skin tone, clean-shaven, piercing black eyes.
- Personality Type: Psychological profile ENTP 7w8. Embedded in skateboarding culture.

